  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the App Layout**\n\nI\'ve got the data structure sorted, and now I\'m shifting focus to the app\'s layout. My aim is a single-view, elegant experience. The plan centers around a top utility bar for quick details and a beautiful, translucent navigation bar. I\'m prioritizing user-friendliness and visual appeal.\n\n\n**Crafting the Hero Section**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the immersive hero section. My current focus is on a stunning background with a smooth gradient and grain, complemented by a sleek header and a quick search bar for easy filtering. I\'m also planning to incorporate elegant key metrics counters within the layout to provide an immediate overview.\n\n\n**Refining the Details**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the detailed modal/sliding drawer. It will include comprehensive vehicle stats like KM, transmission, fuel type, and body type. I\'m also including an estimated monthly finance installment based on a calculated default interest rate and loan term, plus hover animations. I\'m also going to create a browse-by-body-type section with interactive SVG tiles with animations, and am finalizing the financing section with a slick, interactive repayment estimator calculator. Finally, I\'m working on the Sell/Trade-In section.\n\n\n**Developing the Value Section**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the value estimator, and it\'s coming to life! I am building a dynamic form for immediate vehicle appraisal. Users can input brand, year, and mileage, and get an on-screen estimate range. I\'m also planning to allow them to submit the form or share it on WhatsApp. It\'s really turning into a high-fidelity and interactive feature.\n\n\n\n**Implementing the Modals**\n\nI\'m now implementing the slide-up detail modal. Within it, I\'m integrating an image gallery and tabs for an overview, inspection report, and a 360\302\260 view. I\'m also including interactive feature checkboxes, a custom repayment breakdown, and pre-filled WhatsApp enquiry messages. I\'m focusing on ensuring top-notch quality in the implementation. I\'ve verified the required motion packages and completed a successful test import. Now, I\'m preparing to update `src/App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Structuring the App Components**\n\nI\'m now architecting the app\'s core components to ensure modularity and manage potential token limits. I\'m focusing on a clean `/src/App.tsx` and creating reusable sub-components in `/src/components/`. The plan is to build a `Navbar`, `FinanceCalculator`, `TradeInForm`, `VehicleModal`, and `Footer`, each dedicated to a specific function for an intuitive user experience.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` to handle the top utility bar and responsive sticky navigation. It features mobile menu transitions and WhatsApp integration."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 938825047
    }
