  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m focusing now on parsing the user\'s explicit request for a front page mockup, closely reflecting the provided HTML. The key is replicating the \"Cars On Caledon\" design, ensuring accurate branding and colors. Essentially, a single, elegant showcase is what I am aiming to produce.\n\n\n**Refining the Color Scheme**\n\nI\'ve determined the color scheme, focusing on the `--ink`, `--paper`, `--accent`, and `--wa` variables in the HTML. These correspond to charcoal near-black, warm off-white, Caledon crimson, and WhatsApp green, respectively. I\'ve confirmed that the user sent the complete HTML mockup directly, which is a beautifully written front page mockup of \"Cars On Caledon.\" This detailed HTML page includes a navigation bar, a hero section with a background image, and a list of vehicles with filter chips.\n\n\n**Simplifying the Scope**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on the mockup itself, discarding any notions of a full-fledged application. The user clarified they only need the front page, perfectly branded with the correct colors, so I can eliminate unnecessary features. I need to deliver a refined and polished result, not a complex application, just the beautiful front-page mockup.\n\n\n**Connecting the Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the generated components into `/src/App.tsx`. The goal is to build the front page layout, precisely mirroring the original HTML mockup but within our React/Vite environment. The aim is to create a seamless preview by importing and orchestrating `Navbar`, `FinanceCalculator`, `TradeInForm`, `VehicleModal`, and `Footer` within `/src/App.tsx`, which currently is an empty file.\n\n\n**Orchestrating the Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on constructing `/src/App.tsx`, the master component for the front page. My priority is seamless integration of existing components. I\'ll include the `Navbar`, a Hero Section with a background image, a Ticker, and an Inventory Section with filter chips and a car grid, which links to `VehicleModal`. I will carefully review `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` and other components to ensure alignment with the mockup.\n\n\n**Expanding the Design**\n\nI\'m now expanding the `/src/App.tsx` implementation to include the \"Browse by Body Section,\" the Finance, Sell/Trade-in, \"Why Us\", Testimonials, and Contact sections. I\'m focusing on the integration and placement of these components into the mockup, along with the Footer and a floating WhatsApp widget. I\'m also confirming the high-quality car images from `/src/data.ts`.\n\n\n**Managing Component State**\n\nI\'m now focusing on state management within the application. I need to handle filtered vehicles, search parameters (make, body type, max price, sorting), and selected vehicle state for the detail modal. I\'m building handlers to apply filters. I\'ve also confirmed that the Tailwind custom colors are included in the `/src/index.css` file. I\'m building a system to present the active vehicle detail modal.\n\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `/src/App.tsx` to implement the entire, fully functional front page mockup for **Cars on Caledon**. This page will feature our gorgeous header utility bar, custom navigation, an interactive search engine, catalog filters, an inspection grade badge, click-to-open detailed car modals (with interactive 360 walkaround simulator and digital condition checklist), the vehicle repayment estimator, and the trade-in digital appraiser. Let\'s make it look pristine."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 641113067
    }
