    summary: "The search results provide information about the specified car models, including details about their features, performance, and availability, but they do not directly display photos from Unsplash.com. The original query was correctly formatted for a `site:` search on Unsplash.com for images of these car models. Therefore, the summary should acknowledge that the search was performed as requested, but the output from the `google_search` tool does not render the images directly.\n\nThe user\'s query was a direct search on `site:unsplash.com/photos/` for several car models. The search was executed as requested. The provided search results offer general information about some of these car models, such as the 2026 Ford Ranger[1][2], 2026 VW Golf GTI[3], and 2026 BMW M2[4], rather than a direct display of photos from Unsplash.com.\n\nFor example, the Ford Ranger is described as a compact or mid-size pickup truck marketed globally by Ford, with a reintroduction in North America for the 2019 model year[5]. The 2026 Ford Ranger offers a 3.0L EcoBoost\302\256 V6 engine with Auto Start-Stop Technology and a maximum available towing capacity of 7,500 lbs[1]. It is available in a crew-cab configuration with a 5-foot bed and four trim levels: XL, XLT, Lariat, and Raptor[2].\n\nThe 2026 Volkswagen Golf GTI is highlighted as a turbocharged hatchback with a 2.0L TSI\302\256 engine producing 241 hp and 273 lb-ft of torque. It features an available DCC Adaptive Chassis Control and a standard 12.9-inch touchscreen display[3].\n\nThe 2026 BMW M2 is characterized by a twin-turbocharged 3.0-liter inline-six engine, available with either an eight-speed automatic or a six-speed manual transmission. A new M2 CS model for 2026 increases horsepower to 523 and shaves off nearly 100 pounds[4].\n\nWhile these details are provided, the search results do not directly show the requested photos from Unsplash.com.\n\nSources:\n[1] [ford.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/groundi